From: Home Assistant Securo Add-on <noreply@home-assistant.io>
Date: Sat, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(enable-banking): stable fingerprints, duplicate-connection
 adoption, and configurable history window

Four fixes layered on top of upstream v0.16.3 + PR #1074 (stable_id).
None is upstream behaviour, so they are carried as an add-on patch.

1. _txn_fingerprint excludes the session-scoped account_uid. Enable
   Banking mints a new uid per session, so a reauthorization re-keyed
   every transaction into a new external_id and re-imported the whole
   history. #1074 fixes the account row; this fixes its transactions.

2. Duplicate-connection adoption in handle_oauth_callback. A user whose
   consent lapses is routed through Unlink / Connect Bank, so the
   callback arrives with no reconnect_id and a second BankConnection
   row for the same bank. Adopt the stale one, but only when exactly
   one matches and it is not active.

3. enable_banking_history_days (default 999) with strategy="longest".
   Coupled: dropping strategy while keeping 999 makes banks reject the
   window and fall back to FALLBACK_HISTORY_DAYS (30), which is worse
   than upstream's 90.

4. _cleanup_legacy_duplicate_accounts consolidates rows duplicated by
   add-on 0.31.1/0.31.2, which matched on masked_number + currency.
   One-off repair; safe to drop once no install carries those rows.

Reported upstream as issue #1013.
